"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/9f073790-09ec-4392-b284-0723d60a89b7.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":34,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/c52de0c9-3e73-4c1d-939a-e140984bf9c5.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><span>Answer: (a, c)<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span>Solution:<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/05432f98-83f2-427f-a221-434ceb66ecb0.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></span></p>\n<p><span>The correct answer is <strong>(c) Live because x is used in subsequent iterations</strong>.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span>Here's why, based on the principles of <strong>live variable analysis</strong> in compiler optimization:<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span><strong><span>Live Variable Analysis<o:p></o:p></span></strong></span></p>\n<p><span><strong><span>Live variable analysis</span></strong><span> is a <strong>backward</strong> data-flow analysis that determines, for each program point, which variables hold values that may be used later in the program.<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span>A variable V is <strong>live</strong> at a program point P if there is a path from P to a use of V that does not pass through any definition (assignment) of V.<o:p></o:p></span></li>\n<li><span>Otherwise, V is <strong>dead</strong>.<o:p></o:p></span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span><strong><span>Analysis of the Loop<o:p></o:p></span></strong></span></p>\n<p><span>The code snippet is:<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span>while (...) {<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span> x = x + 1; // &lt;-- This is the assignment in question<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span>}<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span>x = 100;<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p><span><span>Let's focus on the assignment </span><strong><span>x = x + 1;</span></strong><span> inside the loop body.<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<ol>\n<li><span><strong><span>Use of x:</span></strong><span> The expression x + 1 <em>uses</em> the current value of x.<o:p></o:p></span></span></li>\n<li><span><strong><span>Subsequent Use:</span></strong><span> In the very next iteration of the </span><span>while</span><span> loop (if the loop condition is still true), the value produced by the assignment (</span><span>x = x + 1;</span><span>) will be <em>used</em> again on the right-hand side of the same assignment statement.<o:p></o:p></span></span></li>\n<li><span><strong><span>Conclusion:</span></strong><span> The value assigned to x in any iteration is immediately needed (and therefore <strong>live</strong>) for the calculation in the next iteration.<o:p></o:p></span></span></li>\n</ol>\n<p><span>Therefore, the assignment to x in the loop body is <strong>Live because x is used in subsequent iterations</strong>.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\n<p></p>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><strong><span>(a) Live because x is the part of Out-set of basic block:</span></strong><span> In the loop body, the statement defines x (new value) and that new value is needed in the next iteration (because the next iteration evaluates x = x + 1 again, using the current x on the RHS).<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><span>In liveness terms, because of the back edge to the loop, x is in the OUT set of the loop-body basic block.<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span>&middot;<span> </span></span><strong><span>(b) Not live because x is assigned a value after loop:</span></strong><span> The assignment </span><span>x = 100;</span><span> <em>after</em> the loop <strong>kills</strong> any previous value of x at that point. However, this is irrelevant to the liveness of x <em>inside</em> the loop for its own iterative computation.<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\n<p><span> <strong><span>(d) Live because x is the part of In-set of basic block:</span></strong><span> The In-set is the set of variables live <em>upon entry</em> to the block. x will be in the In-set because it's used inside the block, but again, option (c) is the best description of the <strong>cause</strong> of its liveness for this specific assignment.</span></span></p>\n<p></p>\n<p></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":35,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B,C,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/a7474766-9484-48a2-b3e1-554eb2b5b1fb.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/48eabdcb-4bbf-414d-8022-2906e7aecc52.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":36,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/316b6cad-6897-46a1-9c3a-4d48307d8167.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<p>a</p>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<p>b</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<p>c</p>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<p>d</p>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/6ba3c207-7ac1-4fc1-8195-d187549769fe.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Computer Science Engineer"},{"qnum":37,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"https://cms-cdn.classplus.co/parserImages/31e403d5-3bc0-4b40-bb53-23f5cc4201b0.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","opti